'''Bosses''' are powerful, usually unique [[monster]]s that are fought to accomplish an objective, be it the completion of a [[quests|quest]] or [[minigames|minigame]], or as part of [[player versus monster]] activities. Many quests feature boss fights at their climaxes; such bosses are often the main antagonists of the quest series or are somehow related to the main antagonists.

Bosses are very powerful monsters that are commonly fought by players, both in teams and alone, in search of highly valuable drops. Many bosses have extremely high [[combat level]]s, and all of the [[strongest monster]]s in the game are bosses. Bosses are typically immune to a combination of either stun, poison, or reflect damage. Even fewer bosses are immune to a combination of leeching effects (from the Ancient Curses) or status abnormalities (defence drain (not affinity value) or damage increasing hexes), generally recovering from the latter very quickly.

Older, traditional bosses such as [[General Graardor]] usually reward their [[drops]] to the player who dealt the most damage, while other bosses, such as [[Vorago]] or [[Nex, Angel of Death]], may also give drops to vital non-damaging roles, such as taking the boss' aggression and/or attacks. Most bosses that are often fought in a group (such as raids and elite dungeon bosses) generally have participants receive their own individual drop as long as they dealt some damage.

[[Dwarf multicannon]]s and [[combat dummy MKII|combat dummies]] often cannot be set up in the areas of many bosses.

Since the introduction of [[Kerapac, the bound]], most updates that introduce new bosses to the game start a week-long event where [[Death]] provides free item reclaims. The event ends at noon seven days after the update that introduces the boss. The release of [[Rasial, the First Necromancer]] and [[Hermod, the Spirit of War]] was an exception, as no free death week occurred during the week of release.

Defeating every boss at least once completes the achievement [[Reaper Crew]], unlocking the title {{TitleAnchor|the Reaper}} and permanently boosting some of the player's combat stats.

